'''Renegades''' was a professional gaming organization, founded in March 2015 under the name [[:leagueoflegends:Misfits_(North_American_team)|Misfits]]. Originally a League of Legends team, the organisation rebranded as '''Renegades''' on June 18, 2015, and picked up the former [[:counterstrike:Vox Eminor|Vox Eminor]] roster for their own CS:GO squad. On August 30, 2016, [[wikipedia:Jonas Jerebko|Jonas Jerebko]] bought the organization from Christopher "[[:overwatch:MonteCristo|MonteCristo]]" Mykles and Chris Badawi. <ref name="Jonas Jerebko bought Renegades">{{cite web|url=http://www.espn.com/esports/story/_/id/17421412/renegades-revived-celtics-forward-jonas-jerebko|date=2016-08-30|title=Renegades revived under Celtics forward Jonas Jerebko|author=Darren Rovell|publisher=[[ESPN]]}}</ref> He is the third [[wikipedia:National_Basketball_Association|NBA]] player to publicly acquire a stake in an esports organization after [[wikipedia:Rick Fox|Rick Fox]] ([[Echo Fox]]) and [[wikipedia:Shaquille O'Neal|Shaquille O'Neal]] ([[NRG Esports]]).

